---
layout: "base"
title: "Instructor lesson plan"
---


<article class="lesson-plan content-column">
	<header class="stacked">
		<nav class="lesson-nav" aria-label="Lesson navigation">
			<a href="/lessons/">All lessons</a>
			<a :href="$data.pagination.href.previous" webc:if="$data.pagination.href.previous">Previous day</a>
			<a :href="$data.pagination.href.next" webc:if="$data.pagination.href.next">Next day</a>
		</nav>
		<eyebrow @text="$data.title"></eyebrow>
		<h1 class="lesson-heading">Week <span @text="$data.lesson.week"></span>, Day <span @text="$data.lesson.day"></span></h1>
		<p class="lesson-when separators">
			<span @text="$data.lesson.display"></span>
			<span @text="timeOfDay($data.lesson.time)"></span>
			<span webc:if="$data.lesson.meeting">Class meeting #<span @text="$data.lesson.meeting"></span> of the term</span>
		</p>
	</header>

	<callout webc:if="$data.lesson.noClass">
		<p>No class on <span @text="$data.lesson.noClass"></span>. Use this day to prep the next lesson or catch up on grading.</p>
	</callout>

	<template webc:nokeep webc:if="!$data.lesson.noClass">
		<p class="focus"><strong>Focus:</strong> <span @text="$data.lesson.focus"></span></p>
		<callout :type="'warn'" webc:if="$data.lesson.substitution">
			<p>This meeting runs a <strong @text="$data.lesson.substitution"></strong> schedule (college-wide) — plan the substituted day's session, not this weekday's usual rhythm.</p>
		</callout>
		<callout :type="'warn'" webc:if="$data.lesson.testWeek">
			<p>A test is scheduled this week — confirm day, reserve class time, and remind students at least one meeting ahead.</p>
		</callout>

		<section aria-labelledby="topics-heading">
			<h2 id="topics-heading">This week's topics</h2>
			<ul>
				<li webc:for="topic of $data.lesson.topics" @raw="topic"></li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="before-heading">
			<h2 id="before-heading">Before class</h2>
			<ul class="checklist" role="list">
				<li webc:if="$data.lesson.readings?.length || $data.lesson.meetingReadings?.length">Review the readings (see materials below)</li>
				<li>Prepare/update slides and live-demo code</li>
				<li webc:for="deck of $data.lessonDecks">Print or open the <a :href="deck.notesUrl">speaker notes sheet</a></li>
				<li>Stage starter files or lab handout if needed</li>
				<li>Check <span @text="$data.site.lms"></span> for student questions or submissions</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="outline-heading">
			<h2 id="outline-heading">Lesson outline (<span @text="$data.lesson.minutes"></span> minutes)</h2>
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr><th scope="col">Time</th><th scope="col">Segment</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr webc:for="row of $data.lesson.outline">
						<td @text="`${row.minutes} min`"></td>
						<td @text="row.segment"></td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="materials-heading">
			<h2 id="materials-heading">Materials &amp; links</h2>
			<link-section webc:for="section of $data.lessonMaterials" :@title="section.title" :@items="section.items" :@empty="section.empty"></link-section>
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="after-heading">
			<h2 id="after-heading">After class</h2>
			<ul class="checklist" role="list">
				<li>Post handouts to <code>content/resources/</code> and link them in <code>_data/schedule.json</code>'s <code>resources[]</code> for the week; the slide deck publishes itself from <code>content/slides/</code>, so it only needs a link there if students should see it from the schedule</li>
				<li>Note anything not covered and roll it into the next lesson</li>
				<li>Post or grade lab/homework in <span @text="$data.site.lms"></span> as needed</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</template>
</article>
